Description: Jmol's display as a declared 3D area on Sparky Stereo OS
 With Enable 3D (Display menu, on by default) the application runs Jmol's own
 side-by-side stereo, "stereo 5" with "set perspectiveDepth false" (the preset:
 the left eye's picture on the left, no vertical difference between the eyes),
 lets Jmol draw each of the two pictures at the display panel's own size, and
 puts them into an X11 window of its own inside the frame, two pictures wide,
 declared to Stereo KWin as full side by side with libstereo-declare
 (stereo_declare_x11_child, the size one view is shown at). The rest of the
 frame stays an ordinary 2D window. Jmol keeps its own stereo angle. A
 negative angle (cross-eyed, Jmol's "stereo on") is handed over left eye
 first. Display gains "Enable 3D" and "3D display settings..."; the popup
 menu's "Stereographic" submenu, whose entries are output modes, is not
 offered; every script command is unchanged.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-21
